                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>SHADOWLOAD</name>
                <description>Shadow load control register.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x128</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SHDLDREQ</name>
                    <description>Shadow load request for each evaluation window (bit index = window index).
Writing a '1' to a bit will load the shadows into the active configuration for that window at start of next frame.
Writing a '0' has no effect. The flag is reset by HW once the shadows have been loaded.
A shadow load interrupt signal is generated when shadows have been loaded for at least one evaluation window.
Has only effect when ShdLdSel is set to LOCAL.</description>
                    <bitRange>[7:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>CONTINUOUSMODE</name>
                <description>Signature operation mode control.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x12C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>ENCONT</name>
                    <description>EnCont = 0: disables continuous mode.
Signatures will be generated only once and in idle state after completion of measurement.
In this 'ONE_TIME' mode the signature must be triggered by 'Kick' field.
EnCont = 1: enables continuous mode.
Write '1' to this field, signature starts and measures every incoming frame until EnCont is turned to 0.
'Kick' has no effect when 'EnCont' = 1.</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>SOFTWAREKICK</name>
                <description>Signature measurement trigger.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x130</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>write-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>KICK</name>
                    <description>ContinueMode.EnCont=0: Write '1' to this field in order to start signature computation with next frame.
ContinueMode.EnCont=1: This field is ignored.</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>STATUS</name>
                <description>Module status.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x134</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x100000</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1100FF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>STSSIGERROR</name>
                    <description>Error status bits for all evaluation windows (bit index = window index).
When a bit is set it means that measured signature value is different from reference value (SigCRCRef).
The bit is set when EnCRC is active and a certain number of frames have a violation (ErrThres).
It is reset when the reference check for evaluation window is disabled (EnEvalWin or EnCRC) or in case a certain number of consecutive frames have no violation (ErrThresReset).
The value corresponds to the panic status of this evaluation window.</description>
                    <bitRange>[7:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>STSSIGVALID</name>
                    <description>Measured signature values are valid.
This flag is set when the SigCRC fields have been updated for all enabled evaluation windows. In that case also the corresponding interrupt event is triggered.
It is reset when SW writes a '1' to the 'Kick' field in order to start a new measurement.</description>
                    <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>STSSIGIDLE</name>
                    <description>StsSigIdle = 1: Signature is in Idle state.
StsSigIdle = 0: Signature runs.</description>
                    <bitRange>[20:20]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
            </cluster>
            <cluster>
              <name>FRAMEGEN1</name>
              <description>Frame Generator</description>
              <addressOffset>0x00002000</addressOffset>
              <register>
                <name>FGSTCTRL</name>
                <description>FrameGen Static Control Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x7</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SHDEN</name>
                    <description>Enables shadowing for RWS type configuration fields.
Otherwise shadow registers are immediately updated when written.</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>FGSYNCMODE</name>
                    <description>Determines the operating mode of the framegen unit for side-by-side synchronization.
The framegen unit programmed as master generates synchronization pulses.
The framegen units programmed as slaves are synchronized to the master unit.
There must be only one framegen unit programmed acting as master.</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:1]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>OFF</name>
                        <description>No side-by-side synchronization.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>MASTER</name>
                        <description>Framegen is master.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SLAVE_CYC</name>
                        <description>Framegen is slave. Runs in cyclic synchronization mode.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SLAVE_ONCE</name>
                        <description>Framegen is slave. Runs in one time synchronization mode.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>HTCFG1</name>
                <description>FrameGen Horizontal Timing Config Register 1</description>
                <addressOffset>0x4</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x18F0140</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3FFF3FFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>HACT</name>
                    <description>Horizontal size of active display area in pixels.
Hact shall be greater or equal than 4.
Note: Valid setup for horizontal video timing contains parameters Hact, Htotal, Hsbp and, if enabled, Hsync.</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>HTOTAL</name>
                    <description>Total horizontal size of frame in pixels.
(Set value +1 is the total horizontal size of frame)
Htotal shall be greater or equal than Hact + Hsbp.
Note1: Valid setup for horizontal video timing contains parameters Hact, Htotal, Hsbp and, if enabled, Hsync.
Note2: If SRAdj==1 then Htotal[0] shall be equal the value of SREven (for sec. channel only).</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>HTCFG2</name>
                <description>FrameGen Horizontal Timing Config Register 2</description>
                <addressOffset>0x8</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x8047001F</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xBFFF3FFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>HSYNC</name>
                    <description>Width of HSYNC pulse in pixels.
(Set value +1 is the width of HSYNC pulse)
HSYNC is of zero width if HsEn==0.
Note: Valid setup for horizontal video timing contains parameters Hact, Htotal, Hsbp and, if enabled, Hsync.</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>HSBP</name>
                    <description>Width of HSYNC pulse plus width of horizontal back porch in pixels.
(Set value +1 is the width of HSYNC pulse plus width of horizontal back porch)
Hsbp shall be greater or equal than Hsync.
Note: Valid setup for horizontal video timing contains parameters Hact, Htotal, Hsbp and, if enabled, Hsync.</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>HSEN</name>
                    <description>Enables generation of HSYNC pulse.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>VTCFG1</name>
                <description>FrameGen Vertical Timing Config Register 1</description>
                <addressOffset>0xC</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0xFC00F0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3FFF3FFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>VACT</name>
                    <description>Vertical size of active display area in lines.
Vact shall be greater or equal than 4.
Note: Valid setup for vertical video timing contains parameters Vact, Vtotal, Vsbp and, if enabled, Vsync.</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>VTOTAL</name>
                    <description>Total vertical size of frame in lines.
(Set value +1 is the total vertical size of frame)
Vtotal shall be greater or equal than Vact + Vsbp.
Note: Valid setup for vertical video timing contains parameters Vact, Vtotal, Vsbp and, if enabled, Vsync.</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>VTCFG2</name>
                <description>FrameGen Vertical Timing Config Register 2</description>
                <addressOffset>0x10</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x80090003</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xBFFF3FFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>VSYNC</name>
                    <description>Width of VSYNC pulse in lines.
(Set value +1 is the width of VSYNC pulse)
VSYNC is of zero width if VsEn==0.
Note: Valid setup for vertical video timing contains parameters Vact, Vtotal, Vsbp and, if enabled, Vsync.</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>VSBP</name>
                    <description>Width of VSYNC pulse plus width of vertical back porch in lines.
(Set value +1 is the width of VSYNC pulse plus width of vertical back porch)
Vsbp shall be greater or equal than Vsync.
Note: Valid setup for vertical video timing contains parameters Vact, Vtotal, Vsbp and, if enabled, Vsync.</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>VSEN</name>
                    <description>Enables generation of VSYNC pulse.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>INT0CONFIG</name>
                <description>Coordinates of the trigger point for generation of the Int0 interrupt signal</description>
                <addressOffset>0x14</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xBFFFBFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT0COL</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which column of the display raster the Int0 signal is triggered (1 .. Int0Col .. HTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining Int0Col (1 .. Int0Col .. HTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT0HSEN</name>
                    <description>When enabled, Int0Row setting is ignored so that the interrupt occurs every line at position given by Int0Col.</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT0ROW</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which row of the display raster the Int0 signal is triggered (1 .. Int0Row .. VTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining Int0Row (1 .. Int0Row .. VTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT0EN</name>
                    <description>Enables Int0.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>INT1CONFIG</name>
                <description>Coordinates of the trigger point for generation of the Int1 interrupt signal</description>
                <addressOffset>0x18</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xBFFFBFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT1COL</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which column of the display raster the Int1 signal is triggered (1 .. Int1Col .. HTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining Int1Col (1 .. Int1Col .. HTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT1HSEN</name>
                    <description>When enabled, Int1Row setting is ignored so that the interrupt occurs every line at position given by Int1Col.</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT1ROW</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which row of the display raster the Int1 signal is triggered (1 .. Int1Row .. VTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining Int1Row (1 .. Int1Row .. VTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT1EN</name>
                    <description>Enables Int1 (irq[1]).</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>INT2CONFIG</name>
                <description>Coordinates of the trigger point for generation of the Int2 interrupt signal</description>
                <addressOffset>0x1C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xBFFFBFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT2COL</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which column of the display raster the Int2 signal is triggered (1 .. Int2Col .. HTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining Int2Col (1 .. Int2Col .. HTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT2HSEN</name>
                    <description>When enabled, Int2Row setting is ignored so that the interrupt occurs every line at position given by Int2Col.</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT2ROW</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which row of the display raster the Int2 signal is triggered (1 .. Int2Row .. VTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining Int2Row (1 .. Int2Row .. VTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT2EN</name>
                    <description>Enables Int2.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>INT3CONFIG</name>
                <description>Coordinates of the trigger point for generation of the Int3 interrupt signal</description>
                <addressOffset>0x20</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xBFFFBFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT3COL</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which column of the display raster the Int3 signal is triggered (1 .. Int3Col .. HTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining Int3Col (1 .. Int3Col .. HTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT3HSEN</name>
                    <description>When enabled, Int3Row setting is ignored so that the interrupt occurs every line at position given by Int3Col.</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT3ROW</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which row of the display raster the Int3 signal is triggered (1 .. Int3Row .. VTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining Int3Row (1 .. Int3Row .. VTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INT3EN</name>
                    <description>Enables Int3.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>PKICKCONFIG</name>
                <description>Coordinates of the trigger point for generation of the primary kick signal</description>
                <addressOffset>0x24</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0xF00140</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xBFFFBFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>PKICKCOL</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which column of the display raster the pkick signal is triggered (1 .. PKickCol .. HTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining PKickCol (1 .. PKickCol .. HTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>PKICKINT0EN</name>
                    <description>If enabled, maps the primary kick signal (pkick) on the interrupt pin int0. Overrides int0en.</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>PKICKROW</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which row of the display raster the pkick signal is triggered (1 .. PKickRow .. VTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining PKickRow (1 .. PKickRow .. VTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>PKICKEN</name>
                    <description>Enables pkick signal.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>SKICKCONFIG</name>
                <description>Coordinates of the trigger point for generation of the secondary kick signal</description>
                <addressOffset>0x28</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0xF00140</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFFFFBFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SKICKCOL</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which column of the display raster the skick signal is triggered (1 .. SKickCol .. HTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining SKickCol (1 .. SKickCol .. HTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SKICKINT1EN</name>
                    <description>If enabled, maps the secondary kick signal (skick) on the interrupt pin int1. Overrides int1en.</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SKICKROW</name>
                    <description>Specifies on which row of the display raster the skick signal is triggered (1 .. SKickRow .. VTOTAL).
Adaptive display timing must be taken into account when defining SKickRow (1 .. SKickRow .. VTOTAL_MIN).</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SKICKTRIG</name>
                    <description>Select source for skick generation.</description>
                    <bitRange>[30:30]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>INTERNAL</name>
                        <description>Use internal skick signal, trigger point defined by SKickRow and SKickCol.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>EXTERNAL</name>
                        <description>Use external skick input as trigger.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SKICKEN</name>
                    <description>Enables generation of internal skick signal.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>SECSTATCONFIG</name>
                <description>Configuration register for controlling the behavior of the SecSyncStat field in the FgSecChStat register.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x2C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x112</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>LEVGOODFRAMES</name>
                    <description>Number of continuous correct frames that must be processed before SecSyncStat field goes 1 (in sync).
Value of 0 is not allowed.</description>
                    <bitRange>[3:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>LEVBADFRAMES</name>
                    <description>Not used.</description>
                    <bitRange>[7:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>LEVSKEWINRANGE</name>
                    <description>Number of continuous frames the measured skew value shall be within the range defined by SyncRangeLow and SyncRangeHigh.
If this condition is true, additionally LevGoodFrames valid frames must be processed before the status line of the sec. channel
and the SecSyncStat status field goes to 1 indicating synchronized status.
Value of 0 is not allowed.</description>
                    <bitRange>[11:8]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSRCR1</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Regulation Control Register 1.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x30</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x301FF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SREN</name>
                    <description>If enabled, skew control for secondary channel is active.
If disabled, skew control for secondary channel is in fetch mode.
Fetch mode: secondary channel fetches frames and can intentionally produce a backstall via setting sbusy signal to active.
This mode is intended to fetch frames from memory via a stallable pipeline, like the primary interface.
No timing adaption of frames takes place in this mode.</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SRMODE</name>
                    <description>Skew Control Operating Mode.</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:1]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>OFF</name>
                        <description>Skew Regulation is off.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>HREG</name>
                        <description>Horizontal regulation enabled.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>VREG</name>
                        <description>Vertical regulation enabled.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BOTH</name>
                        <description>Both regulation modes are enabled.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SRADJ</name>
                    <description>Enables line length adjustment for HTOTAL.
If SRQAlign=0, SREven determines whether HTOTAL has odd (SREven=0) or even (SrEven=1) number of pixels.
If SRQAlign=1, SRQVal determines the value of the two LSB bits of HTOTAL.</description>
                    <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SREVEN</name>
                    <description>Total line length HTOTAL is even when SRAdj is enabled.
Note: This has impact on the settings for Htotal, HtotalMin and HtotalMax.</description>
                    <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SRFASTSYNC</name>
                    <description>Fast Synchronization Mode.
Frame Generator is started synchronized to frame timing on secondary channel when switching FgEn from 0 to 1.
This allows fast locking of skew regulation.</description>
                    <bitRange>[5:5]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SRQALIGN</name>
                    <description>Enables alignment of HTOTAL to be a multiple of 4. Overrides SREven field.
Program field SRQVal for the desired value of the two LSB bits of HTOTAL.</description>
                    <bitRange>[6:6]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SRQVAL</name>
                    <description>If SRQAlign is enabled, this field determines the fixed value of the two LSB bits of HTOTAL.
Note: This has impact on the settings for Htotal, HtotalMin and HtotalMax.</description>
                    <bitRange>[8:7]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ZERO</name>
                        <description>Fixed two LSB values of HTOTAL are 0b00.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE</name>
                        <description>Fixed two LSB values of HTOTAL are 0b01.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>TWO</name>
                        <description>Fixed two LSB values of HTOTAL are 0b10.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>THREE</name>
                        <description>Fixed two LSB values of HTOTAL are 0b11.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SRDBGDISP</name>
                    <description>If enabled, the pixels are displayed that are read from FIFO when secondary channel is not in sync yet.
Otherwise constant color is displayed in unsynchronized state.</description>
                    <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SREPOFF</name>
                    <description>Disables the skew Extrapolation in blanking.</description>
                    <bitRange>[17:17]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSRCR2</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Regulation Control Register 2</description>
                <addressOffset>0x34</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x1B70188</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3FFF3FFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>HTOTALMIN</name>
                    <description>Minimum value of htotal when horizontal regulation is enabled.
(Set value +1 is the minimum value of htotal,
must be greater or equal Hsbp + Hactive)
HTotalMin must be smaller or equal Htotal.
Note: If SRAdj==1 then HtotalMin[0] shall be equal to the value of SREven.</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>HTOTALMAX</name>
                    <description>Maximum value of htotal when horizontal regulation is enabled.
(Set value +1 is the maximum value of htotal)
HTotalMax must be greater or equal Htotal.
Note: If SRAdj==1 then HtotalMax[0] shall be equal to the value of SREven.</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSRCR3</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Regulation Control Register 3</description>
                <addressOffset>0x38</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x11500FB</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3FFF3FFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>VTOTALMIN</name>
                    <description>Minimum value of vtotal when vertical regulation is enabled.
(Set value +1 is the minimum value of vtotal,
must be greater or equal Vsbp + Vactive + 1)</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>VTOTALMAX</name>
                    <description>Maximum value of vtotal when vertical regulation is enabled.
(Set value +1 is the maximum value of vtotal)</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSRCR4</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Regulation Control Register 4</description>
                <addressOffset>0x3C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0xC8</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1FFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>TARGETSKEW</name>
                    <description>Horizontal target skew value for horizontal and vertical skew regulation (signed value).
(format is signed integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[28:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSRCR5</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Regulation Control Register 5</description>
                <addressOffset>0x40</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1FFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SYNCRANGELOW</name>
                    <description>Sync range of horizontal and vertical skew regulation. Lower value (signed value).
If skew stays within programmed sync range, frame status is assumed synchronized.
(format is signed integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[28:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSRCR6</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Regulation Control Register 6</description>
                <addressOffset>0x44</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x190</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1FFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SYNCRANGEHIGH</name>
                    <description>Sync range of horizontal and vertical skew regulation. Upper value (signed value).
If skew stays within programmed sync range, frame status is assumed synchronized.
(format is signed integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[28:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGKSDR</name>
                <description>FrameGen Kick System Debug Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x48</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x20002</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x70007</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>PCNTCPLMAX</name>
                    <description>Maximum Value for ppendcnt_cpl_s complementary primary kick counter. Do not change!</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SCNTCPLMAX</name>
                    <description>Maximum Value for spendcnt_cpl_s complementary secondary kick counter. Do not change!</description>
                    <bitRange>[18:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>PACFG</name>
                <description>FrameGen Primary Area Config Register 1 (shadowed)</description>
                <addressOffset>0x4C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x10001</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3FFF3FFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>PSTARTX</name>
                    <description>Primary screen upper left corner, x component. Counts from 1. Pstartx = 0 is not allowed.
Primary screen shall not overlap the last column/ last row of the total frame defined by Htotal/ Vtotal.</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>PSTARTY</name>
                    <description>Primary screen upper left corner, y component. Counts from 1. Pstarty = 0 is not allowed.
Primary screen shall not overlap the last column/ last row of the total frame defined by Htotal/ Vtotal.</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>SACFG</name>
                <description>FrameGen Secondary Area Config Register 1 (shadowed)</description>
                <addressOffset>0x50</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x10001</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3FFF3FFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SSTARTX</name>
                    <description>Secondary screen upper left corner, x component. Counts from 1 . Sstartx = 0 is not allowed.
Secondary screen shall not overlap the last column/ last row of the total frame defined by Htotal/ Vtotal.
When skew regulation feature is enabled, the secondary screen shall not overlap the active display area defined by Hact and Vact.</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SSTARTY</name>
                    <description>Secondary screen upper left corner, y component. Counts from 1 . Sstarty = 0 is not allowed.
Secondary screen shall not overlap the last column/ last row of the total frame defined by Htotal/ Vtotal.
When skew regulation feature is enabled, the secondary screen shall not overlap the active display area defined by Hact and Vact.</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGINCTRL</name>
                <description>FrameGen Input Control Register (shadowed)</description>
                <addressOffset>0x54</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x6</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1F</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>FGDM</name>
                    <description>Frame Generator Display Mode.</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BLACK</name>
                        <description>Black color background is shown on the whole screen area.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>CONSTCOL</name>
                        <description>Programmable constant color is shown in the active area and black color in the blanking area.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>PRIM</name>
                        <description>Primary input only is shown.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SEC</name>
                        <description>Secondary input only is shown.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>PRIM_ON_TOP</name>
                        <description>Both inputs overlaid with primary on top.</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SEC_ON_TOP</name>
                        <description>Both inputs overlaid with secondary on top.</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>TEST</name>
                        <description>White color background with test pattern is shown in the active area and black color in the blanking area.</description>
                        <value>6</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BLEND</name>
                        <description>Blending of the mode PRIM with the mode SEC.</description>
                        <value>7</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ENPRIMALPHA</name>
                    <description>When enabled, alpha plane of primary channel is considered for screen composition.
If the alpha component of the current pixel is 255, this pixel is opaque.
Otherwise this pixel is transparent.
Setting this field to 1 has no effect, when FgDm == BLEND.</description>
                    <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ENSECALPHA</name>
                    <description>When enabled, alpha plane of secondary channel is considered for screen composition.
If the alpha component of the current pixel is 255, this pixel is opaque.
Otherwise this pixel is transparent.
Setting this field to 1 has no effect, when FgDm == BLEND.</description>
                    <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGINCTRLPANIC</name>
                <description>FrameGen Input Control Panic Register (shadowed)</description>
                <addressOffset>0x58</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x6</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1F</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>FGDMPANIC</name>
                    <description>Frame Generator Display Mode.</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BLACK</name>
                        <description>Black color background is shown on the whole screen area.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>CONSTCOL</name>
                        <description>Programmable constant color is shown in the active area and black color in the blanking area.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>PRIM</name>
                        <description>Primary input only is shown.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SEC</name>
                        <description>Secondary input only is shown.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>PRIM_ON_TOP</name>
                        <description>Both inputs overlaid with primary on top.</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SEC_ON_TOP</name>
                        <description>Both inputs overlaid with secondary on top.</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>TEST</name>
                        <description>White color background with test pattern is shown in the active area and black color in the blanking area.</description>
                        <value>6</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BLEND</name>
                        <description>Blending of the mode PRIM with the mode SEC.</description>
                        <value>7</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ENPRIMALPHAPANIC</name>
                    <description>When enabled, alpha plane of primary channel is considered for screen composition.
If the alpha component of the current pixel is 255, this pixel is opaque.
Otherwise this pixel is transparent.
Setting this field to 1 has no effect, when FgDmPanic == BLEND.</description>
                    <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ENSECALPHAPANIC</name>
                    <description>When enabled, alpha plane of secondary channel is considered for screen composition.
If the alpha component of the current pixel is 255, this pixel is opaque.
Otherwise this pixel is transparent.
Setting this field to 1 has no effect, when FgDmPanic == BLEND.</description>
                    <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGCCR</name>
                <description>FrameGen Constant Color Register (shadowed)</description>
                <addressOffset>0x5C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x1FFFFFF</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1FFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>CCBLUE</name>
                    <description>Constant color - blue component.</description>
                    <bitRange>[7:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>CCGREEN</name>
                    <description>Constant color - green component.</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:8]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>CCRED</name>
                    <description>Constant color - red component.</description>
                    <bitRange>[23:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>CCALPHA</name>
                    <description>Constant color - alpha value. In case of blending the value of 1 will be extended to 0xff.</description>
                    <bitRange>[24:24]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>BLENDCONTROL</name>
                <description>Options for blend operations. (shadowed)</description>
                <addressOffset>0x60</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x1010</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFF7777</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>PRIM_C_BLD_FUNC</name>
                    <description>Primary (background) input color blending function</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ZERO</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * 0</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * 1</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>PRIM_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * ALPHA_prim</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_PRIM_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * (1 - ALPHA_prim)</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SEC_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * ALPHA_sec</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_SEC_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * (1 - ALPHA_sec)</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>CONST_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * ALPHA_const</description>
                        <value>6</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_CONST_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * (1 - ALPHA_const)</description>
                        <value>7</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SEC_C_BLD_FUNC</name>
                    <description>Secondary (overlay) input color blending function</description>
                    <bitRange>[6:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ZERO</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * 0</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * 1</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>PRIM_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * ALPHA_prim</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_PRIM_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * (1 - ALPHA_prim)</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SEC_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * ALPHA_sec</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_SEC_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * (1 - ALPHA_sec)</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>CONST_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * ALPHA_const</description>
                        <value>6</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_CONST_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Cout = Cin * (1 - ALPHA_const)</description>
                        <value>7</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>PRIM_A_BLD_FUNC</name>
                    <description>Primary (background) input alpha blending function</description>
                    <bitRange>[10:8]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ZERO</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * 0</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * 1</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>PRIM_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * ALPHA_prim</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_PRIM_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * (1 - ALPHA_prim)</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SEC_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * ALPHA_sec</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_SEC_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * (1 - ALPHA_sec)</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>CONST_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * ALPHA_const</description>
                        <value>6</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_CONST_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * (1 - ALPHA_const)</description>
                        <value>7</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SEC_A_BLD_FUNC</name>
                    <description>Secondary (overlay) input alpha blending function</description>
                    <bitRange>[14:12]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ZERO</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * 0</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * 1</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>PRIM_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * ALPHA_prim</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_PRIM_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * (1 - ALPHA_prim)</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SEC_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * ALPHA_sec</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_SEC_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * (1 - ALPHA_sec)</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>CONST_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * ALPHA_const</description>
                        <value>6</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ONE_MINUS_CONST_ALPHA</name>
                        <description>Aout = Ain * (1 - ALPHA_const)</description>
                        <value>7</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>BLENDALPHA</name>
                    <description>Constant alpha value, used for constant alpha blending</description>
                    <bitRange>[23:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGENABLE</name>
                <description>FrameGen Enable Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x64</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>FGEN</name>
                    <description>Frame Generator Enable.
Note: For loading the shadow registers at start-up of FrameGen unit write
the FgSlr.ShdTokGen field immediately before writing this field.</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSLR</name>
                <description>FrameGen Shadow Load Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x68</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>write-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SHDTOKGEN</name>
                    <description>Generate shadow load token.
Can be used to load shadow register in this and/or all subsequent units up to the next token end point.</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGENSTS</name>
                <description>FrameGen Enable Status Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x6C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>ENSTS</name>
                    <description>Indicates the current operating mode of the frame generator.
EnSts = 0 means frame generator is disabled.
EnSts = 1 means frame generator is enabled.
In contrast to the FgEn field of the FgEnable register this bit goes only 0
when all pending frames are processed.</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>PANICSTAT</name>
                    <description>Current status of panic mode (0=normal operation mode, 1=panic mode; not locked).</description>
                    <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGTIMESTAMP</name>
                <description>Time stamp status.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x70</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>LINEINDEX</name>
                    <description>Index of the output line that is currently generated (starts with 0 for first active output line).</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>FRAMEINDEX</name>
                    <description>Index of the output frame that is currently generated (starts with 0 after reset for first output frame).
Wraps around to 0 when maximum value is reached.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:14]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGCHSTAT</name>
                <description>FrameGen Channel Status Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x74</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1030101</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>PFIFOEMPTY</name>
                    <description>Read request to empty primary pixel FIFO detected. (Bit locked when 1, clear by using ClrPrimStat).</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>PRIMSYNCSTAT</name>
                    <description>Current status primary channel synchronization (0 = out of sync (frame tearing), 1 = in sync (normal operation); not locked).</description>
                    <bitRange>[8:8]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SFIFOEMPTY</name>
                    <description>Read request to empty secondary pixel FIFO detected. (bit locked when 1, clear by using ClrSecStat).</description>
                    <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SKEWRANGEERR</name>
                    <description>The secondary channel skew value has run out of the limit defined by SyncRangeLow and SyncRangeHigh. (bit locked when 1, clear by using ClrSecStat).</description>
                    <bitRange>[17:17]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SECSYNCSTAT</name>
                    <description>Current status secondary channel synchronization (0 = out of sync, 1 = in sync; not locked).</description>
                    <bitRange>[24:24]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGCHSTATCLR</name>
                <description>FrameGen Channel Status Clear Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x78</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>write-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x10001</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>CLRPRIMSTAT</name>
                    <description>Clears PFifoEmpty in FgChStat register.</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>CLRSECSTAT</name>
                    <description>Clears SFifoEmpty and SkewRangeErr in FgChStat register.</description>
                    <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSKEWMON</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Monitor Register for Secondary Channel Skew Control</description>
                <addressOffset>0x7C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1FFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SKEWMON</name>
                    <description>Current skew value monitor for secondary channel skew control. Updated with hlast.
(For debugging purposes only).</description>
                    <bitRange>[28:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSFIFOMIN</name>
                <description>FrameGen Secondary FIFO Min Fill Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x80</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x0</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SFIFOMIN</name>
                    <description>Shows the minimal fill level of the secondary channel pixel FIFO.
(For debugging purposes only).</description>
                    <bitRange>[10:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSFIFOMAX</name>
                <description>FrameGen Secondary FIFO Max Fill Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x84</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x0</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SFIFOMAX</name>
                    <description>Shows the maximal fill level of the secondary channel pixel FIFO.
(For debugging purposes only).</description>
                    <bitRange>[10:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSFIFOFILLCLR</name>
                <description>FrameGen Secondary FIFO Fill Clear Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x88</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>write-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SFIFOFILLCLR</name>
                    <description>Write for clearing register FgSFifoMin and FgSFifoMax.
(For debugging purposes only).</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSREPD</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Regulation ExtraPolation Debug Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x8C</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1FFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>EPVAL</name>
                    <description>Calculated value for line skew extrapolation in blanking.
Updated with condition 'hlast AND vlast'.
(For debugging purposes only)</description>
                    <bitRange>[28:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGSRFTD</name>
                <description>FrameGen Skew Regulation Frame Total Debug Register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x90</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>FRTOT</name>
                    <description>Measured value for frame total measured in display clock cycles.
Updated with condition 'hlast AND vlast' when first FrTot value is valid.
(For debugging purposes only)</description>
                    <bitRange>[27:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>FGTGPOSITION</name>
                <description>Current (x,y) positions of the timing generator Register in FrameGen timing generator. Please don't use it due to lack of verification.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x94</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>FRTGX</name>
                    <description>Coordinated pixel position starting from HACT inside a total line generated in timing generator in display clock cycles.
(For debugging purposes only)</description>
                    <bitRange>[13:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>FRTGY</name>
                    <description>Coordinated line position starting from VACT inside a total frame generated in timing generator in display clock cycles.
(For debugging purposes only)</description>
                    <bitRange>[27:14]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
            </cluster>
            <cluster>
              <name>GAMMACOR1</name>
              <description>Gamma Correction Unit</description>
              <addressOffset>0x00002400</addressOffset>
              <register>
                <name>STATICCONTROL</name>
                <description>Static control settings.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0xE</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SHDEN</name>
                    <description>Enables shadowing of all RWS type registers (0=write_through, 1=shadowed).</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>BLUEWRITEENABLE</name>
                    <description>Write enable for the blue color sampling point entries.</description>
                    <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>GREENWRITEENABLE</name>
                    <description>Write enable for the green color sampling point entries.</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>REDWRITEENABLE</name>
                    <description>Write enable for the red color sampling point entries.</description>
                    <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>LUTSTART</name>
                <description>Start values for look-up table programming.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x4</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>write-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3FFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>STARTBLUE</name>
                    <description>Start value for blue or chroma (V) channel.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[9:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>STARTGREEN</name>
                    <description>Start value for green or chroma (U) channel.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[19:10]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>STARTRED</name>
                    <description>Start value for red or luma (Y) channel.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:20]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>LUTDELTAS</name>
                <description>Delta values for look-up table programming.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x8</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>write-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x0</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>DELTABLUE</name>
                    <description>Delta value for blue or chroma (V) channel.
(format is signed integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[9:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>DELTAGREEN</name>
                    <description>Delta value for green or chroma (U) channel.
(format is signed integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[19:10]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>DELTARED</name>
                    <description>Delta value for red or luma (Y) channel.
(format is signed integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[29:20]</bitRange>
                    <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>CONTROL</name>
                <description>Dynamic control settings.</description>
                <addressOffset>0xC</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x31</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>MODE</name>
                    <description>Operation mode for gamma correction unit</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>NEUTRAL</name>
                        <description>Module in neutral mode, input data is bypassed to the output.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>GAMMACOR</name>
                        <description>Module in gamma correction mode.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ALPHAMASK</name>
                    <description>Value 1 enables the alpha mask mode. In this mode all pixels with an alpha value smaller than 0.5 are by-passed unchanged.</description>
                    <bitRange>[4:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ALPHAINVERT</name>
                    <description>Value 1 inverts the effect of the alpha mask mode when enabled (pixels with alpha value greater or equal 0.5 are by-passed).</description>
                    <bitRange>[5:5]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
            </cluster>
            <cluster>
              <name>DITHER1</name>
              <description>Dither Unit</description>
              <addressOffset>0x00002800</addressOffset>
              <register>
                <name>CONTROL</name>
                <description>Dither Unit common control.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x1</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>MODE</name>
                    <description>Mode which switches Dither Unit on/off.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>NEUTRAL</name>
                        <description>Neutral mode. Pixels by-pass the Dither Unit, all other settings are ignored.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ACTIVE</name>
                        <description>Dither Unit is active.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>DITHERCONTROL</name>
                <description>Dither Unit processing control.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x4</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x300222</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3310777</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>BLUE_RANGE_SELECT</name>
                    <description>Mode which sets the reduction of component widths.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BLUE_10TO8</name>
                        <description>Reduces blue component width from 10 bit to 8bit.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BLUE_10TO7</name>
                        <description>Reduces blue component width from 10 bit to 7bit.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BLUE_10TO6</name>
                        <description>Reduces blue component width from 10 bit to 6bit.</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BLUE_10TO5</name>
                        <description>Reduces blue component width from 10 bit to 5bit.</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>GREEN_RANGE_SELECT</name>
                    <description>Mode which sets the reduction of component widths.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[6:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>GREEN_10TO8</name>
                        <description>Reduces green component width from 10 bit to 8bit.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>GREEN_10TO7</name>
                        <description>Reduces green component width from 10 bit to 7bit.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>GREEN_10TO6</name>
                        <description>Reduces green component width from 10 bit to 6bit.</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>GREEN_10TO5</name>
                        <description>Reduces green component width from 10 bit to 5bit.</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>RED_RANGE_SELECT</name>
                    <description>Mode which sets the reduction of component widths.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[10:8]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RED_10TO8</name>
                        <description>Reduces red component width from 10 bit to 8bit.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RED_10TO7</name>
                        <description>Reduces red component width from 10 bit to 7bit.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RED_10TO6</name>
                        <description>Reduces red component width from 10 bit to 6bit.</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RED_10TO5</name>
                        <description>Reduces red component width from 10 bit to 5bit.</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>OFFSET_SELECT</name>
                    <description>Selects the method how the dither offset is calculated.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>OFFS_SPATIAL</name>
                        <description>Offset is a bayer matrix value, which is selected according to pixel frame position.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>OFFS_TEMPORAL</name>
                        <description>Offset is the sum from a bayer matrix value, which is selected according to pixel frame position, and a value from a regular sequence, which changes each frame.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ALGO_SELECT</name>
                    <description>The number of output colors that can virtually be displayed by dithering is slightly lower than the number of physical input colors. This field selects how the mapping is done.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[21:20]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>NO_CORRECTION</name>
                        <description>Best possible resolution for most dark colors. Adds a diminutive offset to overall image brightness.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BRIGHTNESS_CORRECTION</name>
                        <description>Preserves overall image brightness. Cannot resolve most dark and most bright colors. All codes in-between are distributed perfectly smooth.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>CONTRAST_CORRECTION</name>
                        <description>Preserves overall image brightness. Best possible distribution of color codes over complete range.</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ALPHA_MODE</name>
                    <description>Enables/disables that dithering can be switched by alpha bit.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[25:24]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>DISABLE</name>
                        <description>The alpha bit is not considered.</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ENABLE_BY1</name>
                        <description>Red, green and blue components are only dithered, if the alpha bit is 1.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>ENABLE_BY0</name>
                        <description>Red, green and blue components are only dithered, if the alpha bit is 0.</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>RELEASE</name>
                <description>Dither Unit release.</description>
                <addressOffset>0x8</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-only</access>
                <resetValue>0x1</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SUBVERSION</name>
                    <description>Dither Unit subversion.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[7:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>VERSION</name>
                    <description>Dither Unit version.
(format is unsigned integer)</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:8]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-only</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
            </cluster>
            <cluster>
              <name>TCON1</name>
              <description>Timing Controller</description>
              <addressOffset>0x00003000</addressOffset>
              <register>
                <dim>64</dim>
                <dimIncrement>4</dimIncrement>
                <name>SSQCNTS[%s]</name>
                <description>The 64 Sequencer Position Definitions registers define the X/Y scan positions of the sequencers, hold their output value and assign the sequencer to an odd/even field</description>
                <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x0</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SSQCNTS_SEQY</name>
                    <description>Y scan position</description>
                    <bitRange>[14:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SSQCNTS_FIELD</name>
                    <description>Field  0b=odd field, 1b=even field</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:15]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SSQCNTS_SEQX</name>
                    <description>X scan position</description>
                    <bitRange>[30:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>SSQCNTS_OUT</name>
                    <description>This bit holds the value (0,1) to be output when the X/Y scan position is reached.</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>SSQCYCLE</name>
                <description>This bitfield sets the sequencer cycle length. The value set here -1 is the number of sequencer cycles</description>
                <addressOffset>0x400</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3F</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SSQCYCLE</name>
                    <description>Sequencer cycle length (number -1) of sequencer cycles</description>
                    <bitRange>[5:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>SWRESET</name>
                <description>TCON Software Reset - Reset all tcon registers except configuration registers. Detailed description in specification document Note  1/ if tsig[11] pulse=n*pixel_period, (n-1)*0xFF will be blended between ResetWordStart and ResetWordEnd into miniLVDS stream  Note  2/ if( EnResetWord=0) Reset-Pulse (ResetWordStart,ResetWordEnd) won't be blended into miniLVDS stream. Pixels will be transferred unchanged</description>
                <addressOffset>0x404</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x3FC00410</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0xFFFFFFF1</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>SWRESET</name>
                    <description>Software reset</description>
                    <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>OPERATION</name>
                        <description>operation mode</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SWRESET</name>
                        <description>So long SWReset = 0x1 tcon is in 'SW reset state' and it is released by internal logic (SWReset is released and end of frame arrived), read  0b  reset not active 1b  reset active (that means NO pixel of video frame is excepted until 'SW reset state' is released)</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>ENRESETWORD</name>
                    <description>Enable to blend ResetWord into miniLVDS stream 
EnResetWord[5-0]  mapped to enable Blending Reset Pulse to [RLV5.RLV0]. 
EnResetWord[11-6] mapped to enable Blending Reset Pulse to [LLV5.LLV0].</description>
                    <bitRange>[15:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>RESETWORDEND</name>
                    <description>8-Bits value, that will be blended on falling edge of tsig[11] into miniLVDS stream</description>
                    <bitRange>[23:16]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>RESETWORDSTART</name>
                    <description>8-Bits value, that will be blended on rising edge of tsig[11] into miniLVDS stream</description>
                    <bitRange>[31:24]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                  </field>
                </fields>
              </register>
              <register>
                <name>TCON_CTRL</name>
                <description>TCON Control register</description>
                <addressOffset>0x408</addressOffset>
                <size>32</size>
                <access>read-write</access>
                <resetValue>0x1401408</resetValue>
                <resetMask>0x3FFFFFFF</resetMask>
                <fields>
                  <field>
                    <name>CHANNELMODE</name>
                    <description>Selects one of tcon operation modes, SINGLE, DUAL_INTERLEAVED or DUAL_SPLIT.
If MiniLVDS operation is selected (EnLVDS = ENABLE_LVDS and LVDSMode = Mini_LVDS), tcon operates in MiniLVDS mode, independent of ChannelMode programming. 
SplitPosition must be specified in MiniLVDS operation 
in DUAL_INTERLEAVED or DUAL_SPLIT mode, the horizontal parameter of signal generator have to set twice as they are specified in the panel-specification 
(panel  320, tsig_start 0, tsig_stop 320 on DUAL-Mode   tsig_start 0, tsig_stop 640 ... (SplitPosition is automatically adjusted) )</description>
                    <bitRange>[1:0]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>SINGLE</name>
                        <description>Single pixel mode. Both channels channel are active at full pixel clock. If bitmap of both panels are the same, both panels are identical</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>DUAL_INTERLEAVED</name>
                        <description>Dual pixel mode. Both channels are active at half the pixel clock. 1st channel drives display columns with even and 2nd one with odd index.</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>DUAL_SPLIT</name>
                        <description>Dual pixel mode. Both channels are active at half the pixel clock. 1st channel drives the left and 2nd one the right half of the display. Note   data_en is needed in this mode</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>TCON_SYNC</name>
                    <description>Select synchronization between hsync/vsync and hlast/vlast</description>
                    <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>H_VLAST</name>
                        <description>tcon timing generator synchronized to hlast, vlast</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>H_VSYNC</name>
                        <description>tcon timing generator synchronized to hsync, vsync where horizontal synchronization is synchronized at the falling edge of hsync</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>BYPASS</name>
                    <description>Bypassing synchronization</description>
                    <bitRange>[3:3]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>TCON_MODE</name>
                        <description>tcon operation mode</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>BYPASS_MODE</name>
                        <description>tcon in Bypass mode. input pixel and its sync-signals are bypassed to tcon-output</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                    </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                    <name>INV_CTRL</name>
                    <description>Minimize the toggle rate of tcon output for display panel, that supports data inversion control. Otherwise set Inv_Ctrl = 0.  
 Valid for all channels .  
 Inv_Ctrl does not effect any function on LVDS-Output.</description>
                    <bitRange>[7:4]</bitRange>
                    <access>read-write</access>
                    <enumeratedValues>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>DISABLE</name>
                        <description>Disable inversion control</description>
                        <value>0</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RGB_2_BITS</name>
                        <description>Enable inversion control for number of RGB-Bits = 2</description>
                        <value>1</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RGB_4_BITS</name>
                        <description>Enable inversion control for number of RGB-Bits = 4</description>
                        <value>2</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RGB_6_BITS</name>
                        <description>Enable inversion control for number of RGB-Bits = 6</description>
                        <value>3</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RGB_8_BITS</name>
                        <description>Enable inversion control for number of RGB-Bits = 8</description>
                        <value>4</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
                        <name>RGB_10_BITS</name>
                        <description>Enable inversion control for number of RGB-Bits = 10</description>
                        <value>5</value>
                      </enumeratedValue>
                      <enumeratedValue>
