                  <description>See RD1_CTL.PC_MASK_0.</description>
                  <bitRange>[16:16]</bitRange>
                  <access>read-only</access>
                </field>
                <field>
                  <name>PC_MASK_15_TO_1</name>
                  <description>Protection context mask for protection contexts '15' downto '1'. Bit PC_MASK_15_TO_1[i] indicates if the GFX_MPU_WRx WR_CTL.PC[3:0] protection context field can be set to the value 'i+1': - PC_MASK_15_TO_1[i] is '0': GFX_MPU_WRx WR_CTL.PC[3:0] can NOT be set to 'i+1'; and PC[3:0] is not changed. If the protection context of the write transfer is '0', protection is not applied and PC[3:0] can be changed. - PC_MASK_15_TO_1[i] is '1': GFX_MPU_WRx WR_CTL.PC[3:0] can be set to 'i+1'.

Note: When CPUSS_CM0_PC_CTL.VALID[i] is '1' (the associated protection context handler is valid), write transfers to PC_MASK_15_TO_1[i-1] always write '0', regardless of data written. This ensures that when valid protection context handlers are used to enter protection contexts 1, 2 or 3 through (HW modifies CPUSS_PROT_MPU0 MS_CTL.PC[3:0] on entry of the handler), it is NOT possible for SW to enter those protection contexts (SW modifies GFX_MPU_WRx WR_CTL.PC[3:0]).</description>
                  <bitRange>[31:17]</bitRange>
                  <access>read-write</access>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
